  "caption": "Quinn bought a walking pad, waved goodbye to the chair, and by day three had typo-filled emails and a sore back.\n\nA walking pad can modestly cut down sitting time, but it replaces sitting, not exercise, and it isn't a treatment for back or neck pain on its own.\n\nWhat often helps: walking during calls, reading and email, and sitting or standing still for precise typing; setting the desk at standing height with elbows near 90 degrees, the screen at eye level and a separate keyboard; keeping regular strength sessions; and mixing walking, standing and sitting.\n\nVertigo, balance problems or a recent leg injury? Check before using one. Chest pain, one-sided calf swelling or new leg weakness needs prompt assessment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
